// Teuval

#define DETAIL_TEXT_SANITARIUM "\"The rumour circles that the reason for the uncommon scale, grandeur and complexity of the facilities of the Sanitarium is the interesting popularity of the Town with Psydonian pilgirms. \n\ Those devoted men and women of the Old Faith flocked to the Town, as a resting stop before pilgrimaging out to the Weeping Grove, and then further south towards the Unforgotten Fortress. \n\ But the roads and paths of the Grove oft times proved dangerous and treacherous, and with their own faith standing inbetween their broken bodies and the grace of the Ten Saints, they found themselves in need for a more impartial place of healing. \n\
With time, the clergy of the Otavan Orthodoxy finally managed to gather the funds to construct a marvelous, stone hall, meant for a group of more.. religiously tolerant healers. \n\ Conflict with local religious authorities soon arose. The local clergymen disliked the power slipping from their grasp, and soon they strongarmed the Ducal Family into permitting the Sanitarium be built outside the Walls of the Town."
#define DETAIL_TEXT_PILFIELD "\"Although at first sight it might seem that the Village of Pilgrim's Field is infact, simply a continous part of the City of Teuval, only, outside of the protection of it's stony walls, the small Village is in it's own, covolutedly-legalese way, a completely separate entity. \n\ The Town, in the past and in the present and, hopefully also in the future, tends to enjoy a steady and sizeable amount of Psydonite Pilgirms, looking out to pay their respects at the now-swamped entrance to the Unforgotten Fortress. \n\ In time, the local Clergy devoted to the Worship of the Ten grew tired and ired at the continous and unashamed romancing of the political and economical elite, and the unending masses of, what in their mind were, blasphemous fools. \n\
Threathening to petition the Holy See for a more direct intervention, the local Tennite clergy managed to finally push the ruling family into outlawing the presence of Psydonites within the city limits. \n\ The Pilgrims, unabashed and greatly unwilling to stop their travels to their rememberance sites, simply began setting up tents and shanty towns directly outside the city walls. \n\ With time, the opportunities that the presence of the Psydonites provided, greatly outshined any potential ire that the clergy could dish out at the Town's merchant class, and booths and smaller shops began setting up outside of the city walls, servicing the many faithful found therein. \n\
With the coming of reign of Queen Alexia, blessed be her name, The Tyrant forever guiding her reign, the agreements with the Holy Mission of the Otavan Orthodoxy, to most known simply as the Otavan Inquisition, also mandated the reversal of the ban on the presence of Psydonites within the city. Although by that point, Pilgirm's Field, as it came to be known, was already a prospering village. \n\ It is said, albeit that's more a rumour than ensured fact- that the Soldiers of the Most Holy Orthodoxy came to know the County yils before the Blessed Queen even came within grasp of the Crown of Ferentia..."
#define DETAIL_TEXT_FORGOTTENTEMPLE "He... can't really be dead, can He..?"
#define DETAIL_TEXT_TEUVAL "\"Teuval is a County, with its capital located in the Town bearing the same name. Although the name of the County comes from the name of the Town. \n\ The County of Teuval is, de jure, part of the Duchy of Rockhill, albeit, due to being a potential breeding ground for religious conflict, Kingsfield's eye is focused upon it much more often when comapred to its peers. \n\ The Elves claim that the Town- or at least the region immediately surrounding it, was once home to an ancient druidic cult, focused around worshipping, and preserving the Grove, before it had yet wept. \n\ Psydonite pilgrims headed to the Weeping Grove, and Noccite scholars heading towards the Bluewater Forests are the lyfeline of the Town, and quite probably only the reason why it's not yet abandonded. \n\ Religious conflict is common occurence within the County, The Comital family oft being forced to act as mediators between the Psydonites and Tennites. \n\
The name, 'Teuval' although rumoured by the more wondrous folk to come from Estruscan Merchantry who were said to visit the town often, is in full actuality simply a bastardization of 'Twae-Hylls-Vale'. As yils passed, Aeon consumed 'Hylls' and mangled 'Twae' to 'Teu', and so 'Teuval' was born."
#define DETAIL_TEXT_TEUVAL_KEEP "\"The Castle of Teuval was originally erected hundred of yils ago, as a personal retreat for the Ferentian Royalty, since then, countless disputes, treaties, backstabbings and all the other possible political games that have been played, left it as a semi-independent County under the Duchy of Rockhill. This is why the Teuval Keep is much larger and more grandeur in its design when compared to other Comital holdings. \n\ The size of the Teuval Keep is often times used by the local nobility as a reason to boast and bragg about their supposed power and wealth. It is also, possibly even more often, used as a reason to insult them, citing their supposed need to 'compensate' for 'something'. "
#define DETAIL_TEXT_RAVOX_DUNGEON_ENTRANCE "\"The Father of Knowledge once tasked a group of faithful Ravoxian Templars with the creation of a glorious fortress, able to hold and contain unholy artyfacts. And so the Order of Saint Deryvis was born. \n\ Noc once whispered horrible predictions of coming catastrophes into the ear of a respected Ravoxian Templar, and claimed that only the knowledge hidden within the unholy could possibly save Grimoria. And so the Order of Saint Deryvis was born. \n\ A chivalrous group of Ravoxian knights once arrived to Teuval, and when they witnessed the beauty of the Grove, they all bent the knee to the local Lord and swore to protect it with their very own lyves. And so the Order of Saint Deryvis was born. \n\ The Fool of all Knowledge once sacrificed an entire chapter of Ravoxian Templars, all in a vain effort to stop a miniscule part of HER Grand Plan. And so the Order of 'Saint' Deryvis was born. \n\ When a group of Noccite scholars realized what could potentially hide within the deepest encraoches of the Forgotten Fortress, they frantically begged the Holy See to send a contingent of Knights to take control of the Grove, and guard the secret. And so the Order of Saint Deryvis was born."
#define DETAIL_TEXT_WEEPING_GROVE "\ The name 'Weeping Grove' comes from the pre-rotten tymes, when PSYDON still yet walked the earth with mortals, he once stumbled upon this grove, and when he bore witness to the indescribable beauty within, he wept, and where his tears fell, new lyfe sprung up, providing a rich bounty for the Elves of the local villages. \n\ The name 'Weeping Grove' comes from the fact, that when PSYDON was mortally struck by ZIZO, the river cutting across the entire grove bled out clear and pure water through the surrounding forests, and into the Sea."
#define DETAIL_TEXT_NOCCITE_MOUNTAIN "\"And so the Father of All-Knowledge set upon, claiming the highest mountain in the region for his magnificient and dazzling fortress of bluestone, its rooms filled with the greatest and most innovative laboraties and scholarly spaces, and atop this grand construct, a spiring tower of white marble, from the top of which, He surveyed the lands and watched the Fortress of the Worshippers of his FATHER - and the ever-crawling tidal wave of rot intent on marching on- and claiming all HOPE that yet dwelled down within... \n\ The Arch-lych laughed, and commanded her undead hordes to step in fast order upon the magnificient fortress, to stop the Moon-Father, to claim the last bit of HOPE yet remaining... And so the Father found- and tricked his Maddened Brother - Dendor, into breathing out his very own inspiration into the barren fields afore the fortress- and alas! A grand and magnificient growth of wylderness exploded out of the very soil, trapping the unwilling soldiers of HER deep within the creeping tree-trunks... \n\
The Dame of Damnation sighed at the foolish resistance- and with the whisper of her horrid, creeking voice promised upon the inhabitants of the Land, unthinkable riches, power, and the ability to defy Necra herself... Within daes a dozen cults sprang up across the region, and the roads and paths of every last Settlement and Town ran scarlet with the flowing incessant blood of the innocent, and the fools enamored by HER lies began a construction of a Grand and Mighty Altar, out of the bone and the flesh and the meat of the murdered.. \n\ Sparing no tyme, NOC ventured out to find The Trickster- falling before the Jester-God upon his very knees and pleading for one, last favour...   ...Within quick moments, upon the oaken desk of the Highest of the Otavan Inquisitiorial Officials, laid a grave and most catastrophic report, decrying the unholy amalgamation under-construct by the sacrilegious masses. Within the week, boats, boasting with regiments of most faithful of the Orthodoxy's Men set out for the stormy, Teuvali shores. \n\
With the rooting out of the Cultists, and the destruction of the Amalgamation- The Father, aware that only the knowledge and the power contained within the Dark Artyfacts of Rot could assist him in stopping the encroaching darkness, NOC, with a deep regret upon knowing what he would need to do, sat atop the firmaments of Heaven when the tyme of nite came, and saw throughout all the lands, looking for a sacrificial lamb... \n\ Within one of the Grenzel Casteels, he found the High Templer, Arvillten, head of a respected Order of Ravoxian Knights. With deep pain punctuating his voice- and shaking breath carrying his speech, he whispered into the valiant man's ear the precognitions of the coming damnation. It worked. And within weeks, the Order of Saint Deryvis was born."
